WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.994
Welcome to Module 1 of the learning
path The Daily Checks on One Dashboard:

2
00:00:04.994 --> 00:00:07.425
one workbook, one tab per daily check.

3
00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:10.460
In about forty minutes, plus
a lab in a test workspace,

4
00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:14.483
you'll see which daily checks a
workbook can show and from which table,

5
00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:17.800
which ones it can only link to,
and how the workbook is kept

6
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.400
as a reviewed file rather than
something edited in the portal.

7
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:24.400
The module has been reviewed and approved.

8
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:29.650
Here's what you'll be able to do.

9
00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:34.400
Name the dashboard options in Azure,
and say why the design is one workbook.

10
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.575
Say, for each daily check, its table
or its link-out, and how well it fits.

11
00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:42.988
Give each source's availability in G C C.

12
00:00:42.988 --> 00:00:45.972
And build the workbook's
template from the manifest,

13
00:00:45.972 --> 00:00:48.262
then validate an export from the portal.

14
00:00:48.262 --> 00:00:52.855
You'll need the operator runbook's chapter
on the daily checks as a prerequisite,

15
00:00:52.855 --> 00:00:55.520
and PowerShell 7 with Pester for the lab.

16
00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:00.095
Unit 1.

17
00:01:00.095 --> 00:01:04.079
Microsoft's guidance compares
workbooks, portal dashboards,

18
00:01:04.079 --> 00:01:09.157
Dashboards with Grafana, which is a preview,
Azure Managed Grafana and Power BI.

19
00:01:09.157 --> 00:01:12.108
Workbooks read the widest
set of Azure data and

20
00:01:12.108 --> 00:01:14.983
can be managed as Resource
Manager templates.

21
00:01:14.983 --> 00:01:19.813
Microsoft 365 has built-in views in
each admin center, but no single

22
00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:24.907
custom dashboard: a view across them
needs their logs in Log Analytics.

23
00:01:24.907 --> 00:01:28.068
So the design is one workbook
in the Sentinel workspace,

24
00:01:28.068 --> 00:01:31.660
and a link out where a check's
data stays in another portal.

25
00:01:35.410 --> 00:01:36.248
Unit 2.

26
00:01:36.248 --> 00:01:42.635
Ten tabs query tables; two link out:
Entra Health, and the I T S M task queue.

27
00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:47.470
Three of the ten are partial: the grants
and admin changes tabs list changes,

28
00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:50.433
but the match to a ticket
stays in the I T S M tool,

29
00:01:50.433 --> 00:01:55.735
and the log review tab shows the queue
while the review stays a recorded procedure.

30
00:01:55.735 --> 00:02:00.414
The synchronization servers and domain
controllers send their event logs

31
00:02:00.414 --> 00:02:04.647
through the Azure Monitor Agent, not
to a file share, one row per server.

32
00:02:04.647 --> 00:02:10.280
On availability: workbooks, Entra and
Intune logs, Defender X D R alerts,

33
00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:14.650
the Azure Monitor Agent and
the Logs Ingestion API are

34
00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.923
all available with a G C C
tenant and commercial Azure.

35
00:02:18.923 --> 00:02:21.633
The Defender portal's
connector overview is a

36
00:02:21.633 --> 00:02:24.272
commercial-cloud preview,
so it isn't assumed.

37
00:02:24.272 --> 00:02:28.680
And Entra Health monitoring and
Connect Health are not yet specified.

38
00:02:32.430 --> 00:02:33.305
Unit 3.

39
00:02:33.305 --> 00:02:37.779
The template is built from the
manifest and one K Q L file per query,

40
00:02:37.779 --> 00:02:42.418
and a validator runs ten checks on
it, or on any export from the portal.

41
00:02:42.418 --> 00:02:44.192
Four matter most in practice.

42
00:02:44.192 --> 00:02:47.504
A widened look-back makes a
month of data look like today's.

43
00:02:47.504 --> 00:02:50.905
One query on another
workspace mixes environments.

44
00:02:50.905 --> 00:02:53.780
Without the banner, a tab reads as proof.

45
00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:57.583
And an export embeds I D's:
Microsoft says to mask them,

46
00:02:57.583 --> 00:03:00.060
and the kit simply fails them.

47
00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:04.872
Who is this for?

48
00:03:04.872 --> 00:03:09.273
Security operations takes the sources,
the template and its validator.

49
00:03:09.273 --> 00:03:13.685
Operators learn which tab shows their
family's check, and which ones link out.

50
00:03:13.685 --> 00:03:18.860
An I S S O reviewer can read the
introduction and summary and skip the labs.

51
00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:23.631
Two federal requirements: the reachability
record supports continuous and system

52
00:03:23.631 --> 00:03:28.198
monitoring, and the validation record
supports the baseline and change control.

53
00:03:28.198 --> 00:03:32.160
The steps support these
controls; the assessor decides.

54
00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:41.748
Lab 1 runs on a laptop with no tenant, in
the developer workbook's Chapters 1 and 2.

55
00:03:41.748 --> 00:03:45.586
You'll list the twelve tabs
and open the Entra Health tab:

56
00:03:45.586 --> 00:03:48.923
a link-out, with no table,
to the Entra admin center.

57
00:03:48.923 --> 00:03:51.384
Then you'll validate a
copy someone exported

58
00:03:51.384 --> 00:03:53.647
after editing the workbook in the portal.

59
00:03:53.647 --> 00:03:57.328
Four edits, four failures:
a query on a workspace path,

60
00:03:57.328 --> 00:04:02.900
a thirty-day look-back, a missing banner,
and a subscription path in the file.

61
00:04:06.650 --> 00:04:11.975
Lab 2 runs in a test workspace, never
production, and the authors haven't run it.

62
00:04:11.975 --> 00:04:16.604
From Chapter 1, list which of the
manifest's tables the test workspace has;

63
00:04:16.604 --> 00:04:19.613
each missing table is a
source still to connect.

64
00:04:19.613 --> 00:04:24.596
From Chapter 2, open the template in
the portal through the Advanced Editor,

65
00:04:24.596 --> 00:04:28.374
save a test copy, edit it, export
it, and validate the export.

66
00:04:28.374 --> 00:04:30.130
Then delete the copy.

67
00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:34.967
Three questions.

68
00:04:34.967 --> 00:04:39.279
First: Entra Health's alerts are a daily
check, so what does their tab show?

69
00:04:39.279 --> 00:04:44.155
A query over the sign-in logs, a link out
to the Entra admin center, or nothing?

70
00:04:44.155 --> 00:04:47.253
It's a link out, because
the alerts aren't in Log

71
00:04:47.253 --> 00:04:51.355
Analytics and their G C C
availability is not yet specified.

72
00:04:51.355 --> 00:04:56.467
Second: an export has the workspace's
path saved in it; which check fails?

73
00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:59.242
Check ten, because the
deployment plan fills

74
00:04:59.242 --> 00:05:01.717
I D's per environment, never the template.

75
00:05:01.717 --> 00:05:06.829
Third: a password reset is in yesterday's
audit log; which tab lists it?

76
00:05:06.829 --> 00:05:10.957
The admin changes tab, where the
operator matches it to its ticket,

77
00:05:10.957 --> 00:05:13.555
and a reset with no
ticket opens a finding.

78
00:05:13.555 --> 00:05:17.106
In summary: every daily check
now has a tab or a link-out,

79
00:05:17.106 --> 00:05:21.867
every source its availability, and
the workbook is a reviewed template.

80
00:05:21.867 --> 00:05:25.810
Module 2 reads it, deploys
it, and keeps the evidence.
